[Music]  we live in a country that has incredible  abundance but if you were to add up all  of the hungry people in Los Angeles  County and it's contiguous counties as  well you'd have a state of hunger the  size of New Mexico or West Virginia two  and a half million people to me it is a  mandate for us to do better around this  and it's so simple it's just sharing  abundance my name is rick timaeus i'm  founder and executive director of food  for word our mission is to recover fresh  produce that would otherwise go to waste  and get it to people in need we started  in 2009 and it really was just walking  around my neighborhood and seeing all  these fruit trees dripping with citrus  that I realized that with a few  volunteers there might be a project here  that I could help facilitate eight and a  half years later and 43 million pounds  later here we are  [Music]  we have fed over one and a half million  people this year we have three programs  backyard harvest literally going into  folks homes who have agreed to have us  in there taking excess produce from  their trees sometimes their Gardens the  second program that was added a couple  years later was farmers market recovery  were at about 24 farmers markets every  single week with volunteer teams and  then the big one is the wholesale  recovery which works kind of under cloak  of darkness we get up super early  usually before the Sun even comes up and  are out there with our trucks gathering  pallets and entire truckloads of food  that is perfectly viable but for  whatever reason without otherwise end up  in a trash dump we're looking at things  that just might have a slight  discoloration or a slight bruise on them  it still has weeks left to its life but  it's not perfect and that's where we get  called  [Music]  we have learned that that hunger hides  in plain sight here in society there  should be no shame around it  unfortunately there is but the more that  we bring abundance out and really give  people food with dignity and give them  quality healthy nutritious food these  issues will slowly go away  [Music]

